# WS6-01 (API conformance). Sources: spec/appendix-stdlib.md and spec/appendix-amiga.md
# (the API tables are the normative surface: name, parameters with modes, result type);
# spec/10-modules.md (an import names a public function of the module).
# Expected: no missing, module, arity, mode, type, or returns report. Every public
# function is mentioned in an appendix (an undocumented export is a WS6-06 consistency
# item, not a conformance failure).
# Each report is reviewed by hand before it becomes a finding: an appendix shorthand
# (a row that lists only modes, a combined row) is a script limit, not a finding.
# Detector: run with --appendix on a copy of appendix-stdlib.md with one name renamed,
# one return type changed, and one mode flipped; all three must be reported.
expect: script
--- output
conformance: 0 report(s); 0 undocumented public function(s)
